# privacy-stop.allow: the reviewed allowlist of privacy-stop.sh. One entry per line, "#<index> <fingerprint> <reason>":
# the index of a word in the sorted name list and the fingerprint of the list it was reviewed against
# (`privacy-stop.sh fingerprint`); never a word, a part of one or a hash of one. An entry whose fingerprint is not the
# current list's is stale and allows nothing. Only root adds or re-reviews an entry, in a reviewed change.
